      "content": "Even a single dose can pose risks when interacting with antipsychotics, so self-medicating is not advisable. Pseudoephedrine can sometimes increase heart rate and blood pressure, which could be complicated by your current medications. The safest course of action is to try to contact your healthcare provider or a telehealth service for guidance on managing your congestion safely.",
      "source": "target",
